  "description": "CUVBUT crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C178 H162 N8 O82 Yb14. From the CIF bond table, Yb1 (Yb) has 9 O neighbors; Yb2 (Yb) has 9 O neighbors; Yb3 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb4 (Yb) has 9 O neighbors; Yb5 (Yb) has 9 O neighbors; Yb6 (Yb) has 9 O neighbors; Yb7 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb8 (Yb) has 9 O neighbors; Yb9 (Yb) has 9 O neighbors; Yb10 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb11 (Yb) has 9 O neighbors; Yb12 (Yb) has 9 O neighbors; Yb13 (Yb) has 9 O neighbors; Yb14 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 14 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.641-3.759 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 92.26-105.10°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Yb14(HL)2L20(DMF)8(H2O)8]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
